                  <p>A <code>role="navigation"</code> attribute is used to define a <code>navigation</code> landmark.</p>

                  <h2>ARIA Example: One Navigation Landmark</h2>
                  <p>When only one navigation landmark on a page, a label is optional.</p>
                  <div class="code">
                    <code>
                    &lt;div <strong>role="navigation"</strong>&gt;<br>
                    <br>
                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&lt;h2&gt;<em>title for navigation area</em>&lt;h2&gt;<br>
                    <br>
                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&lt;ul&gt;<br>
                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="page1.html"&gt;<em>Link 1</em>&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;<br>
                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="page2.html"&gt;<em>Link 2</em>&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;<br>
                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="page3.html"&gt;<em>Link 3</em>&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;<br>
                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="page4.html"&gt;<em>Link 4</em>&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;<br>
                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;.....<br>
                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&lt;/ul&gt;<br>
                    &lt;/div&gt;
                    </code>
                  </div>

